  "notes": "The German remixer who converted acoustic songs into tropical/deep house, and his method is the harmonic parameter: \"he inherits the harmony from the source song — his method is documented as taking an existing acoustic or singer-songwriter record and rebuilding it as an 'up-tempo reimagining', so expect diatonic guitar-song progressions rather than EDM vamps, with maj7/add9 recolouring\". That is why this model carries five major diatonic families with real functional motion and a `1_per_bar` harmonic rhythm, where the EDM models in this section sit on a single static minor vamp. The kit is \"deep-house four-on-the-floor with a soft kick, clap on 2&4, offbeat shakers and 16th percussion loops; no hard drops — the energy curve is flat by design\", which is the low drop-out probability, the ladder off and a shaker/perc/conga bed at 4-7 hits a bar. The documented structural device is \"an instrumental restatement of the vocal hook on that palette after each chorus\", so every structure places a bridge after a hook, and \"arrangements are vocal-forward with the electronic layers underneath\". The bass is \"rounded syncopated sub with deep-house motion, sitting well below the vocal\". ⚠ The research says the tempo and palette come from the sub-genre convention; that mark is repeated here, and the velocities, densities and registers are INFERRED.",
